  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased security along the Zimbabwean-Mozambique border in Gonarezhou National Park, Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project supports park protection activities in Gonarezhou Naitonal Park in Zimbabwe, which houses one of Zimbabwe&apos;s largest remaining elephant populations. Specific activities include the refurbishment of a ranger training center inside the park, basic and specialized training courses for rangers, establishment of a scene-of-the-crime unit to investigate poaching incidents, and operational support for aerial surveillance.</narrative>
  </description>
